 "standard_text": "Determine the square roots of perfect squares and the cube roots of perfect cubes.",
 "meta_desc": "Free Grade 7 square roots and cube roots worksheets for the DepEd MATATAG curriculum: perfect squares, perfect cubes, solving x² = a and word problems. 100 questions with answers.",
 "key_big": "√49 = 7 because 7 × 7 = 49.",
 "key_sub": "∛64 = 4 because 4 × 4 × 4 = 64.",
 "body_html": "<h2>How to think about it</h2><ul><li>A <b>perfect square</b> is a whole number times itself: 49 = 7 × 7. Its <b>square root</b> is √49 = 7.</li><li>A <b>perfect cube</b> is a number used three times as a factor: 64 = 4 × 4 × 4. Its <b>cube root</b> is ∛64 = 4.</li><li>A square with area 81 cm² has sides of √81 = 9 cm. A cube with volume 125 cm³ has edges of ∛125 = 5 cm.</li><li>∛(−27) = −3, because (−3) × (−3) × (−3) = −27.</li></ul><h2>Examples</h2><div class='sn-ex'><span class='sn-ex-t'>Example</span><p class='sn-ex-q'>√144</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>12 × 12 = 144</p><p class='sn-ex-a'>Answer: 12</p></div><div class='sn-ex'><span class='sn-ex-t'>Example</span><p class='sn-ex-q'>∛216</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>6 × 6 × 6 = 216</p><p class='sn-ex-a'>Answer: 6</p></div><h2>Common mistakes</h2><div class='sn-tw'><table class='sn-table'><thead><tr><th>Mistake</th><th>What to do instead</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Dividing by 2</td><td>√64 is 8, not 32.</td></tr><tr><td>Dividing by 3</td><td>∛27 is 3, not 9.</td></tr><tr><td>Squaring as doubling</td><td>5² = 25, not 10.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>",
 "faq": [
  {
   "q": "What does MATATAG Math 7 ask about roots?",
   "a": "Determine the square roots of perfect squares and the cube roots of perfect cubes."
  },
  {
   "q": "Does 49 have two square roots?",
   "a": "Yes, 7 and −7; √49 means the positive one, 7."
  },
  {
   "q": "Can a negative number have a cube root?",
   "a": "Yes. ∛(−8) = −2."
  },
  {
   "q": "Is 50 a perfect square?",
   "a": "No. It is between 49 and 64."
  }
